<section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <h2 id="faq-title">Questions about Twine</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details id="faq-ai-tools">
      <summary>Which AI tools can connect to Twine?</summary>
      <p>Use a tool on your Mac that supports local MCP servers over HTTP and bearer-token authentication. Some tools need a connector or a config file. Twine can copy its connection settings as JSON. Cloud-hosted chat services can't reach your Mac directly. Follow the <a href="/docs#connect-an-ai-tool">connection guide</a> to check your setup.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can an AI tool change my highlights?</summary>
      <p>No. The connection is read-only. A connected tool can read your whole library, so keep the access token private. Turn AI Access off, or regenerate the token, to cut a tool off.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need an account? Where does my data live?</summary>
      <p>There's no Twine account. Your highlights are stored on your devices and sync through your own private iCloud, so the developer never receives them. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> has the details.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-iphone-sync">
      <summary>When do Safari highlights sync between my devices?</summary>
      <p>On Mac, Twine uploads Safari highlights while the app is running. Closing its window doesn't quit it. On iPhone, open Twine after highlighting in Safari so the new highlights can upload to iCloud. Use the same Apple Account on both devices. The <a href="/docs#sync-with-icloud">sync guide</a> explains the steps.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-private-browsing">
      <summary>Does Twine work in Private Browsing?</summary>
      <p>No. Twine doesn't save, show or remove highlights in Private Browsing windows.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it work on every web page?</summary>
      <p>Twine needs selectable text and permission to run on the site in Safari. It leaves text fields alone. Highlights return only when the page's text and surrounding context still match, so changed pages may not show every saved highlight.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need Apple Intelligence?</summary>
      <p>Only to write or refresh an AI context explanation. You can read an explanation that synced from another device without generating it again. Saving highlights, syncing and AI Access don't need Apple Intelligence.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which languages and devices does Twine support?</summary>
      <p>Twine is available in English, German, Spanish, French and Russian, for Mac and iPhone. See the <a href="#requirements">system requirements</a> above. This website is in English for now.</p>
    </details>
